# local env files — never commit secrets.
#
# Ignore EVERY .env variant and un-ignore only the committed template. The old
# rules listed .env and .env*.local by name, which meant a new variant like
# .env.india was not covered — and that file carries a Meta CAPI token, a
# Razorpay webhook secret and the Pabbly URL.
#
# `.env*` rather than `.env` + `.env.*`, because neither of those catches the
# form a browser produces when the same file is downloaded twice:
#
#     .env (2).example        .env (8).local
#
# Both landed in this repo untracked and committable. The next one to arrive
# that way will be somebody's live keys.
.env*
!.env.example
# the dotless typo. Next.js does not load it, so it is easy to create by
# mistake and not notice — and the patterns above do not catch it.
env.local
env*.local

# vercel
.vercel

